From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Hennig <patrick.hennig@uu.se>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: pmk8550: wire RTC set-time via SDAM nvmem
 offset

The pmk8550 RTC counter is write-protected, so rtc-pm8xxx persists a
settable wall-clock time by storing a signed offset in a PMIC SDAM nvmem
cell. With no "offset" cell wired to the RTC node,
pm8xxx_rtc_update_offset() returns -ENODEV and every RTC_SET_TIME fails;
the clock is read-only and stays at its power-on epoch (1970) across
boots, so systohc/NTP can never persist time. This breaks anything that
relies on monotonic wall-clock across reboots (e.g. Steam Cloud save
conflict resolution).

Add an rtc_offset cell in pmk8550_sdam_2 (spare scratch at 0xbc, clear of
reboot_reason@48) and reference it from pmk8550_rtc, matching the wiring
pmk8280-based boards use. The SDAM lives in the PMIC always-on domain
(battery-backed), so the offset — and thus wall-clock time — now
persists across reboots.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Hennig <patrick.hennig@uu.se>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pmk8550.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pmk8550.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pmk8550.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pmk8550.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pmk8550.dtsi
@@ -49,6 +49,8 @@
 			reg = <0x6100>, <0x6200>;
 			reg-names = "rtc", "alarm";
 			interrupts = <0x0 0x62 0x1 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+			nvmem-cells = <&rtc_offset>;
+			nvmem-cell-names = "offset";
 		};
 
 		pmk8550_sdam_2: nvram@7100 {
@@ -62,6 +64,10 @@
 				reg = <0x48 0x1>;
 				bits = <1 7>;
 			};
+
+			rtc_offset: rtc-offset@bc {
+				reg = <0xbc 0x4>;
+			};
 		};
 
 		pmk8550_gpios: gpio@b800 {
